  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Firms, investors and courts pay for careful, explainable valuations. They judge you by the clarity of assumptions and the honesty about uncertainty.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is a simple cash-flow model with stated assumptions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and business valuation careers: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools build template models and summarise filings. Template modelling shrinks first.
  </p>
  <p>
    Choosing assumptions, defending them and owning the report hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI for drafts and checks; later, own the judgment.
  </p>

